  "issue": {
    "body": "Does Starlette support a max message size config option or parameter?\r\n\r\nI've looked through the docs and code and cannot find one.\r\n\r\nIf it does not exist then one should be added. Without such an option a client can perform a memory exhaustion attack on the server simply by sending a huge message.\r\n\r\nOther frameworks have added max message size support for this reason:\r\n\r\n* aiohttp added one: https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/issues/1952\r\n* Sanic has four options: https://sanic.readthedocs.io/en/latest/sanic/websocket.html\r\n* Tornado also has a max_message_size.\r\n\r\nCheers!",
    "closed_at": "2019-02-23T18:42:37Z",
    "created_at": "2019-02-23T16:40:38Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/407",
